Error [E0121]: `xs` was consumed by the move `^xs`, so it can't be used here
  --> ownership_assignment_move_provenance.jet:6:11
    |
  6 |     print(xs.len())
    |           ^^
  --> ownership_assignment_move_provenance.jet:5:10
    |
  5 |     ys = ^xs
    |          ^^^ `xs` moved to the move `^xs` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `xs` after the move, or give the move `^xs` a copy with `xs.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
